Silicon captures from an RTX 3090 driven by the sass-rig harness: ids prefixed s3, s4 and s5 come from rig sessions 3 to 5, the rest from the earlier runs.
One fixture per line, id is <capture>#<index in that capture> and word_hex the instruction, so any case can be re-run on the rig.
observed:true means the outputs were captured on silicon, false marks a case the rig could not run.
mul-add and gradient are whole nvcc-compiled programs with their silicon outputs.
